  "answer_text": "# Welch Allyn Ophthalmology Tools\n\nWelch Allyn is a globally recognized manufacturer of medical diagnostic equipment, offering a comprehensive portfolio of ophthalmic instruments such as ophthalmoscopes, retinoscopes, and vision screeners. Here is an overview of their key ophthalmology tools:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 1. PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope\nThe wide-view Welch Allyn\u00ae PanOptic\u2122 Plus Ophthalmoscope is designed with long-lasting LED lamps and DuraShock\u2122 for durability, plus the new **Quick Eye\u2122 alignment technology** that helps direct the patient's gaze for faster, easier exams. Two lights on the patient side help guide their gaze for better optic disc alignment.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc41\ufe0f 2. Standard Direct Ophthalmoscope (Model 11720-L)\nThe Welch Allyn 11720-L Ophthalmoscope is a classic direct ophthalmoscope used for routine eye examinations. It is a staple tool for general practitioners and ophthalmologists alike.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd26 3. Streak Retinoscope (Model 18245)\nWelch Allyn offers retinoscopes as part of their full range of ophthalmic equipment. The Welch Allyn 18245 Streak Retinoscope is used for objective refraction to determine a patient's refractive error.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcf1 4. iExaminer System / SmartBracket\nThe Welch Allyn **iExaminer SmartBracket** allows clinicians to capture and share eye images when paired with a smart device and the iExaminer Pro App. The PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope with iExaminer system is particularly useful during patient eye exams.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0d 5. Transilluminator (Model 41100)\nThe Welch Allyn 41100 Transilluminator is used to examine the eye and surrounding structures using a focused light source.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udc76 6. Spot Vision Screener\nThe **Spot Vision Screener** is a handheld, portable device designed to help quickly and easily detect vision issues on patients as young as six months. Welch Allyn offers a variety of vision screening devices that are designed to be easy to use and accurate, and can be used by healthcare professionals in schools, doctor's offices, and other settings.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcf8 7. RetinaVue 700 Imager\nAs the latest addition to the RetinaVue care delivery model family, the **RetinaVue 700 Imager** makes retinal imaging and retinal exams simple and affordable in primary care.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd0b 8. Power Handles & Charging Systems\nWelch Allyn offers a **3.5V Premium Lithium Ion Plus USB Rechargeable Power Handle** and a **Universal Desk Charger** to power their diagnostic instruments. All portable ophthalmic sets include ophthalmoscopes with long-lasting LED illumination.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udccb 9. Fixation Cards & Accessories\nWelch Allyn also provides accessories such as **Fixation Cards (Model 18250)** and **Learner Eye Models** (available in black & white and color) for training and patient fixation during exams.\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Tool | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| PanOptic Plus Ophthalmoscope | Wide-field retinal/optic disc viewing |\n| Direct Ophthalmoscope (11720-L) | Standard fundus examination |\n| Streak Retinoscope (18245) | Objective refraction |\n| iExaminer SmartBracket | Digital image capture via smartphone |\n| Transilluminator (41100) | Ocular/tissue transillumination |\n| Spot Vision Screener | Pediatric & adult vision screening |\n| RetinaVue 700 Imager | Retinal imaging in primary care |\n| Rechargeable Power Handles | Powering diagnostic heads |\n| Fixation Cards | Patient fixation during exams |\n\nWelch Allyn (now under **Hillrom/Baxter**) continues to be a leading provider of high-quality ophthalmic diagnostic tools trusted by eye care professionals worldwide.",
